{
  "course": "初中60短文",
  "passage": 33,
  "title": "Passage 33",
  "voice": "温暖自然英式女老师｜IndexTTS2.5 慢速教学",
  "sentences": [
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 1,
      "sourceSentenceId": 1,
      "chunkId": "s33-p01",
      "image": "assets/images/01.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p01.mp3",
      "en": "We use pencils to write and erasers to erase what we've written.",
      "cn": "我们用铅笔写字，用橡皮擦掉写下的字。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 2,
      "sourceSentenceId": 2,
      "chunkId": "s33-p02",
      "image": "assets/images/02.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p02.mp3",
      "en": "But no one knows who invented the pencil or when it was invented.",
      "cn": "但没人知道铅笔是谁发明的，是何时被发明的。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 3,
      "sourceSentenceId": 3,
      "chunkId": "s33-p03",
      "image": "assets/images/03.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p03.mp3",
      "en": "The Swiss Conrad Gesner described a pencil in a book in 1565.",
      "cn": "1565年，瑞士人康拉德·杰斯纳在一本书中描述了铅笔。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 4,
      "sourceSentenceId": 4,
      "chunkId": "s33-p04",
      "image": "assets/images/04.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p04.mp3",
      "en": "Mr Gesner said it was a piece of wood or bamboo with lead inside it.",
      "cn": "杰斯纳先生说，铅笔是里面装着铅的一段木头或竹子。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 5,
      "sourceSentenceId": 5,
      "chunkId": "s33-p05",
      "image": "assets/images/05.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p05.mp3",
      "en": "Pencils weren't popular, and people continued to write with pens.",
      "cn": "铅笔当时并不流行，人们继续用钢笔书写。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 6,
      "sourceSentenceId": 6,
      "chunkId": "s33-p06",
      "image": "assets/images/06.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p06.mp3",
      "en": "They used bird feathers as pens.",
      "cn": "他们把鸟羽作为钢笔使用。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 7,
      "sourceSentenceId": 7,
      "chunkId": "s33-p07",
      "image": "assets/images/07.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p07.mp3",
      "en": "Then, in 1795, some pioneers founded the pencil industry when they started making pencils from graphite chips, and pencils became very popular.",
      "cn": "后来，在1795年，一些先驱者开始用石墨片制作铅笔，从而创立了铅笔行业，铅笔开始大受欢迎。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 8,
      "sourceSentenceId": 8,
      "chunkId": "s33-p08",
      "image": "assets/images/08.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p08.mp3",
      "en": "One pencil can make a line as long as 55 kilometres.",
      "cn": "一支铅笔可以画出一条55千米长的线。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 9,
      "sourceSentenceId": 9,
      "chunkId": "s33-p09",
      "image": "assets/images/09.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p09.mp3",
      "en": "People then used pens with metal points.",
      "cn": "后来人们使用带金属笔尖的笔。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 10,
      "sourceSentenceId": 10,
      "chunkId": "s33-p10",
      "image": "assets/images/10.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p10.mp3",
      "en": "They had to dip the point into ink after every few letters.",
      "cn": "他们每写几个字母就得用笔尖蘸一下墨水。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 11,
      "sourceSentenceId": 11,
      "chunkId": "s33-p11",
      "image": "assets/images/11.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p11.mp3",
      "en": "Next, someone invented a fountain pen that could hold ink inside.",
      "cn": "之后，有人发明了能在内部储存墨水的自来水笔。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 12,
      "sourceSentenceId": 12,
      "chunkId": "s33-p12",
      "image": "assets/images/12.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p12.mp3",
      "en": "A fountain pen can write several pages before you have to fill it again.",
      "cn": "一支自来水笔可以写好几页纸，然后才需要再填充墨水。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 13,
      "sourceSentenceId": 13,
      "chunkId": "s33-p13",
      "image": "assets/images/13.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p13.mp3",
      "en": "Nowadays, there are purple or silver inks that allow you to write in fancy colours.",
      "cn": "如今，有紫色或银色的墨水，可以让你用绚丽的颜色书写。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 14,
      "sourceSentenceId": 14,
      "chunkId": "s33-p14",
      "image": "assets/images/14.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p14.mp3",
      "en": "Two brothers, Ladislao and Georg Biro, invented the ballpoint pen.",
      "cn": "拉迪斯劳和乔治·毕罗两兄弟发明了圆珠笔。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 15,
      "sourceSentenceId": 15,
      "chunkId": "s33-p15",
      "image": "assets/images/15.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p15.mp3",
      "en": "Pilots liked the pens.",
      "cn": "飞行员们喜欢这种笔。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 16,
      "sourceSentenceId": 16,
      "chunkId": "s33-p16",
      "image": "assets/images/16.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p16.mp3",
      "en": "They couldn't write with fountain pens in planes because the ink leaked out.",
      "cn": "他们不能在飞机上使用自来水笔，因为墨水会漏出来。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 17,
      "sourceSentenceId": 17,
      "chunkId": "s33-p17-01",
      "image": "assets/images/17.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p17-01.mp3",
      "en": "Some of today's ballpoint pens have a spring inside,",
      "cn": "现在的一些圆珠笔内部有弹簧，"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 18,
      "sourceSentenceId": 17,
      "chunkId": "s33-p17-02",
      "image": "assets/images/17.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p17-02.mp3",
      "en": "so that you can hide the point when you are not writing.",
      "cn": "以便不写字时可以将笔尖收起来。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 19,
      "sourceSentenceId": 18,
      "chunkId": "s33-p18",
      "image": "assets/images/18.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p18.mp3",
      "en": "Companies use colourful packs, maybe printed with cute animals like rabbits or giraffes, to attract customers.",
      "cn": "商家会使用丰富多彩的包装，上面可能印有可爱的动物图案，如兔子或长颈鹿，以吸引顾客。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 20,
      "sourceSentenceId": 19,
      "chunkId": "s33-p19",
      "image": "assets/images/19.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p19.mp3",
      "en": "Whatever they look like, we see them everywhere on sale and use them every day.",
      "cn": "无论它们长什么样，我们都能看到它们在各处售卖，而且我们每天都在使用着它们。"
    }
  ],
